 is a list","w":0.38683125813802088},{"text":"of irregular verbs on page 142.","y":0.55808477247609012,"x":0.52469135884837304,"w":0.19547324286566836,"h":0.011773940345368938},{"w":0.070380744934082085,"y":0.57636485873343912,"x":0.52859563489064898,"h":0.012967957057982815,"text":"be and go"},{"h":0.013090522173248242,"x":0.52469136119332849,"y":0.5930141285452083,"text":"• The past participle form of be is been:","w":0.25925925360785596},{"x":0.54526749306620537,"text":"Have you ever been really scared?","w":0.21810699462890626,"y":0.61185243312847182,"h":0.011773940345368827},{"y":0.62790697675247376,"w":0.36831275092230897,"h":0.013081394896215293,"text":"• Go has two past participle forms, been and gone, which","x":0.52674897436737778},{"y":0.64244186064528219,"h":0.011796757789384271,"x":0.54320987981057489,"w":0.15637859768337681,"text":"have different meanings:"},{"w":0.35596706814236112,"y":0.65973312418988328,"h":0.011778503609601865,"text":"My parents have been to Italy. (Some time ago. They are","x":0.54320988601626796},{"x":0.54313376500076249,"y":0.67264066684089197,"text":"no longer there.)","h":0.013730294663266029,"w":0.10920572068956169},{"x":0.5432098709876545,"text":"My parents have gone to Italy. (They are still in Italy).","w":0.33333333333333337,"h":0.011773940345368938,"y":0.69034536901747268},{"y":0.70784883719566982,"w":0.36213989257812507,"text":"• We often use been when talking about sports or other","h":0.011627906907110019,"x":0.52469137661903054},{"y":0.72238372106194881,"x":0.543209877536869,"text":"physical activities:","h":0.01162790690711013,"w":0.11934155782063804},{"text":"I've been bungee jumping.","y":0.73979591829278457,"w":0.17078189425998258,"x":0.54320987876164106,"h":0.011773940345368938},{"x":0.52880658533833413,"y":0.75726744190849804,"h":0.010174418169437871,"w":0.10493826972113718,"text":"ever and never"},{"text":"We often use ever and never with the Present Perfect:","h":0.010220053806035412,"x":0.52469136922722959,"y":0.77470930248868219,"w":0.34362138536241316},{"x":0.52469136093793545,"y":0.79199372052655614,"w":0.18312756008572051,"h":0.011785349254518351,"text":"• We use ever in questions:"},{"text":"Have you ever been camping?","y":0.80959302333908068,"w":0.19341562906901044,"h":0.01162790690711013,"x":0.54526749249567308},{"h":0.011773940345368938,"x":0.52469135432929337,"w":0.37242797851562492,"y":0.82692307709338619,"text":"• We use never in negatives. Remember that in sentences"},{"w":0.32304524739583329,"h":0.011627906907110019,"x":0.54115227880551253,"y":0.84011627905613495,"text":"with never, we use the affirmative form of the verb:"},{"y":0.8575353217514019,"h":0.011773940345368938,"text":"Our teacher has never taken us on a school trip.","w":0.30246914333767361,"x":0.54526748972519601},{"x":0.89711934130591875,"y":0.94186046540617996,"h":0.013081394896215293,"text":"133","w":0.034979423946804422}]